    - target: {fileID: 8473876816714486389, guid: 7c4d372918ed05a40996bf0658e7ceca, type: 3}
      propertyPath: artifactTitle
      value: "Tripartite Stone Shiva Linga (\u0E28\u0E34\u0E27\u0E25\u0E36\u0E07\u0E04\u0E4C\u0E28\u0E34\u0E25\u0E32) "
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8473876816714486389, guid: 7c4d372918ed05a40996bf0658e7ceca, type: 3}
      propertyPath: alternateModel
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 631729347}
    - target: {fileID: 8473876816714486389, guid: 7c4d372918ed05a40996bf0658e7ceca, type: 3}
      propertyPath: artifactDescription
      value: '- Period / Dating: c. 7th-8th Century CE (12th-13th Centuries Buddhist
        Era)

        - Material: Carved sandstone

        - Dimensions: Height:
        58 cm | Width: 16 cm | Thickness: 16 cm

        - Discovery Location: Western
        moat area, Ban Prawae Ancient Monument Group, Yarang District, Pattani Province
        (Found in 1977)

        - Current Repository: Art and Cultural Center, Yala
        Rajabhat University



        Curatorial Description:

        This monolithic
        sandstone sculpture is a classic canonical (bap prapheni-niyom) Shiva linga
        sculpted into three equal vertical sections symbolizing the Hindu Trimurti:



        -
        Rudra-bhaga (Top): A smooth, egg-shaped cylinder representing Lord Shiva,
        carved with a vertical central ridge (Brahmasutra) and curved lateral contour
        lines (Parsvasutra) extending toward the rear.

        - Vishnu-bhaga (Middle):
        An octagonal prismatic shaft symbolizing Lord Vishnu, designed to sit within
        a sacred yoni pedestal.

        - Brahma-bhaga (Base): A square prismatic
        block representing Lord Brahma, intended to be anchored into the sanctuary
        foundation.



        The discovery of this artifact provides key material
        evidence of active Shaivite Hindu worship and syncretic religious culture
        flourishing alongside Buddhism within the ancient maritime entrepot of Yarang
        (Langkasuka).'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8473876816714486389, guid: 7c4d372918ed05a40996bf0658e7ceca, type: 3}
      propertyPath: spatialToggleButtonAnchor
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 777709902}
